From c1d9813c5e4eaf8bedff03347a25ea5db2abd96e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@example.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 20:40:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Fix broken install, dead boot sequence, and
 duplicate/unreachable files

- package.json: remove unrar-js@^1.2.0 (version doesn't exist, npm install
  failed outright); promote jszip to a real dependency
- archive.js: rewrite to use jszip for CBZ (bundled, reliable) instead of
  runtime-loading libarchive.js from a CDN; drop the broken unrar-js RAR
  fallback chain in favor of an honest 'not supported, convert to CBZ'
  message
- index.html: rebuild missing <main> markup (CSS had no matching HTML),
  mount the app into #app instead of document.body
- BootScene.js: port the real boot sequence (collision, impact squash,
  camera shake, explosion with debris colored from the bodies' own
  textures, pixel-dissolve wipe, pixel wordmark) -- it was a 1200ms stub
- textures.js: add the planet/flash/particle generators BootScene needs
- TownScene.js: fix showRarHelp being called out of scope (would have
  thrown ReferenceError on every failed RAR upload); gate legacy
  stage-nav buttons behind ?debug=1 instead of always showing dev tooling
- remove dead code: ReaderScene.js (unused duplicate of ReaderPanel.js),
  StageScene.js (iframe-based legacy loader, no longer referenced)
- deduplicate stages/ and legacy-prototype/stages/ (had already drifted --
  one variable name typo differed between copies) into a single copy
- move stages/ and legacy-landing.html into public/ so vite build
  actually includes them in dist/ (they were being silently dropped from
  production builds before)
- tests/cbr.spec.js: update to test the new honest CBR-rejection behavior
  instead of the old 'try to decode regardless of extension' behavior
- add test-results/ and playwright-report/ to .gitignore
