From 050651eed6d113e428cabf479400ecb7643d93a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@example.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 07:39:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Fix fake cover-color analysis: town.js never actually
 used extractDominantColor

Town.addPlot() was coloring every plot by hashing the filename string,
completely ignoring the actual uploaded cover image. extractDominantColor()
existed fully written in color.js and was never called anywhere in the app.
This was the single flagship feature described in docs/DESIGN.md and it
did not run.

- addPlot() now runs extractDominantColor() on the real cover thumbnail
- uses the existing hslToHex/shade helpers instead of ad-hoc color math
- restores the analyze-then-fade-in lamp behavior (380ms delay + 500ms
  fade) instead of snapping the lamp on instantly
